# Entry `quote`, step 1: the total starts as the amount, as a number (the
# query string arrives as text; `&add` coerces). The callee runs on a fresh
# envelope — nothing of the caller's but `@call.input` — so it gates on how
# it was entered, as a capability gates on `@cap.name`.
WHEN @src == "call" && @call.entry == "quote"
  EMIT ._call.output.total = &add(@call.input.amount, 0)
